  "solution": {
    "text": "Tangents drawn from the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>, meet the cirle at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> &amp; <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> be the centre of given circle. Then points <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> are concyclic. That means any circle passing through <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math> also passes through <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is the diameter for this circle. Hence mid point of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is the circumcentre of triangle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></math>.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image38-e1cabffe-1f0f-4198-9ca1-16892bb31728.jpg\" style=\"height: 131px; width: 250px;\" /><br /><br /><br />Coordinates of circumcenter  <math><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
